We switched the sign of the pole‑angle coefficient (params[1]) to negative so the controller pushes opposite to the lean, and also made the angular‑velocity weight (params[3]) negative for proper damping of the pole’s rotation. The cart‑position and cart‑velocity terms (params[0] and params[2]) are kept negative to provide corrective forces when the cart drifts or moves away from the centre. All gains are moderate enough to avoid immediate saturation while still delivering sufficient corrective torque, and we start with zero bias (params[4]) to let the pure feedback dynamics dominate. This sign pattern matches classic negative‑feedback LQR controllers for cart‑pole and should reduce the persistent left/right drift observed in previous runs.
